# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overview {#overview}"
msgstr "نظرة عامة {#overview}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Q-CTRL **Dynamics Simulator** is an application Qiskit Function for simulating the time evolution of supported quantum many-body models on IBM Quantum hardware. Instead of constructing quantum circuits yourself, you specify the physical model, the initial state, the time-evolution parameters, and the observables to measure.\n"
msgstr "إن Q-CTRL **Dynamics Simulator** هي Qiskit Function من نوع Application لمحاكاة التطور الزمني لنماذج الأجسام المتعددة الكمومية المدعومة على عتاد IBM Quantum. وبدلاً من بناء الدارات الكمومية بنفسك، تحدد النموذج الفيزيائي والحالة الابتدائية ومعاملات التطور الزمني والقيم المرصودة المراد قياسها.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The function constructs and executes the required dynamic circuits and applies Fire Opal's hardware-aware optimization and error suppression workflow. The result is a time trace of expectation values for the observables you requested. Because the function applies error suppression automatically, you can run circuits at record depths and still see meaningful signals. The Dynamics Simulator delivers solution accuracy that matches the existing state-of-the-art classical tools and gives a demonstrable advantage in speed.\n"
msgstr "تبني الدالة الدارات الديناميكية المطلوبة وتنفذها، وتطبّق سير عمل Fire Opal للتحسين المراعي للعتاد وكبت الأخطاء. والنتيجة هي أثر زمني لقيم التوقع للقيم المرصودة التي طلبتها. ولأن الدالة تطبّق كبت الأخطاء تلقائياً، يمكنك تشغيل دارات بأعماق قياسية وما زلت ترى إشارات ذات معنى. يقدم Dynamics Simulator دقة حل تضاهي أدوات الحوسبة الكلاسيكية الحديثة الرائدة الحالية، ويحقق ميزة ملموسة في السرعة.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Real-world testing achieved agreement within 1% root mean square error (RMSE) when compared against the highest-resolution classical tensor-network simulations. [Independent tests](https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.04771) from the research community have validated that the quantum computer remains accurate even beyond Q-CTRL's initial demonstrations.\n"
msgstr "حققت الاختبارات الواقعية توافقاً ضمن 1% من جذر متوسط مربع الخطأ (RMSE) عند المقارنة بأعلى محاكاة شبكات التنسور (tensor-network) الكلاسيكية دقةً. وقد أكدت [الاختبارات المستقلة](https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.04771) من المجتمع البحثي أن الحاسوب الكمومي يظل دقيقاً حتى بعد العروض الأولية لـ Q-CTRL.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Two plots of classical tensor-network simulations at bond dimensions χ from 64 to 4096. The left plot shows the RMSE against time t, which stays near 0.01 until it rises sharply, later for larger bond dimensions. The right plot shows the simulation time in minutes against time t on a logarithmic scale, which increases with bond dimension.](/docs/images/guides/q-ctrl-dynamics-simulator/tensor-network-comparison.svg \"Agreement between quantum and classical simulations as the “resolution” of the classical simulation increases. As the resolution increases, both the agreement with the quantum computer and the classical-simulation runtime increase. Quantum computer runtimes are faster by up to 3000 times.\")\n"
msgstr "![Two plots of classical tensor-network simulations at bond dimensions χ from 64 to 4096. The left plot shows the RMSE against time t, which stays near 0.01 until it rises sharply, later for larger bond dimensions. The right plot shows the simulation time in minutes against time t on a logarithmic scale, which increases with bond dimension.](/docs/images/guides/q-ctrl-dynamics-simulator/tensor-network-comparison.svg \"Agreement between quantum and classical simulations as the “resolution” of the classical simulation increases. As the resolution increases, both the agreement with the quantum computer and the classical-simulation runtime increase. Quantum computer runtimes are faster by up to 3000 times.\")\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Benchmarks {#benchmarks}"
msgstr "المعايير المرجعية {#benchmarks}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The number of sites determines how many qubits are needed, while the number of Trotter steps controls the depth of the time-evolution circuits. Each lattice site uses two qubits to represent the spin-up and spin-down occupations.\n"
msgstr "يحدد عدد المواقع عدد الكيوبتات المطلوبة، بينما يتحكم عدد خطوات Trotter في عمق دارات التطور الزمني. يستخدم كل موقع في الشبكة كيوبتين لتمثيل إشغال الاتجاه العلوي (spin-up) والاتجاه السفلي (spin-down).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This workflow has been demonstrated for chains of 60 sites (120 qubits) with 30 Trotter steps, and for chains of 31 sites (62 qubits) with 90 Trotter steps. The table below shows the circuit resources and QPU execution times from the [reported experiments](https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.04025), performed on IBM&reg; Heron r3 (`ibm_boston`) device with 20,000 shots per circuit.\n"
msgstr "تم إثبات سير العمل هذا لسلاسل من 60 موقعاً (120 كيوبت) مع 30 خطوة Trotter، ولسلاسل من 31 موقعاً (62 كيوبت) مع 90 خطوة Trotter. يعرض الجدول أدناه موارد الدارة وأوقات تنفيذ QPU من [التجارب المبلّغ عنها](https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.04025)، والتي أُجريت على جهاز IBM&reg; Heron r3 (`ibm_boston`) مع 20,000 shot لكل دارة.\n"

